// Workout Monitor: ESP32 version
// Live Firebase data over the ESP32's own Wi-Fi on the OLED, with the pot,
// 3 buttons and 2 LEDs. No Yun Shield and no fetch_live.py needed: the ESP32
// downloads /live from Firebase itself and does the same filtering/shortening
// that fetch_live.py used to do (active people only, ASCII text, same limits).
//
// Board:     ESP32 Dev Module (ESP32 DevKit V1), Arduino-ESP32 core 2.x or 3.x
// Libraries (Library Manager):
//   U8g2         by oliver
//   ArduinoJson  by Benoit Blanchon (version 7.x)
//   (WiFi, HTTPClient, WiFiClientSecure come with the ESP32 core)
//
// FILL IN: WIFI_SSID, WIFI_PASS below (2.4 GHz network; the ESP32 can't do 5 GHz).
//
// SET USE_WIFI TO 0 to run the screen on built-in fake people instead (no Wi-Fi
// needed). Handy for testing the buttons, pot, LEDs and buzzer on the bench.
//
// WIRING (the pot and OLED use 3V3. Do NOT connect them to 5V/VIN):
//   OLED   GND->GND, VCC->3V3, SDA->GPIO21, SCL->GPIO22
//   Pot    left->3V3, middle->GPIO34, right->GND
//   Left button   GPIO25 -> GND
//   Middle button GPIO26 -> GND
//   Right button  GPIO27 -> GND
//   LED1 (red)    GPIO18 -> 220 ohm -> LED -> GND
//   LED2 (green)  GPIO19 -> 220 ohm -> LED -> GND
//   Buzzer        (+) -> GPIO4, (-) -> GND   (active 3.3 V buzzer)
//
// UPLOADING: plug the ESP32 in over USB, pick "ESP32 Dev Module" and the port,
// upload. If it hangs on "Connecting...", hold the BOOT button until it starts.
//
// BUTTONS (tap = quick press, hold = about 0.6 s):
//   LEFT    tap: previous page        hold: jump home to the Overview
//   MIDDLE  tap: silence the buzzer   hold: pause / resume live updates
//                (refreshes now when nothing is beeping)
//   RIGHT   tap: next page            hold: jump to the next person who needs help
//   POT     scrolls the rows of the page
//
// LEDS:
//   LED1 (red)    flashes while someone's last rep was wrong, off otherwise
//   LED2 (green)  status: solid = live data OK, slow blink = offline / no Wi-Fi,
//                 off = updates paused (HOLD)
//
// BUZZER (someone keeps doing it wrong):
//   Beeps 3 times every 2 seconds when a person gets ALARM_STREAK wrong reps in a
//   row, or when the database marks them as needing attention. It stops when you
//   press the middle button, or by itself once that person does a correct rep.
//   The person's page shows "Streak: N" (wrong reps in a row) so you can see who set it off.
//
// SCREEN (nothing flashes on refresh):
//   * Header turns white              = this person's last rep was wrong
//   * Bar on a row's left edge        = a problem (wrong rep, form issue, attention)
//   * "+2" in the header              = 2 OTHER pages changed since you looked
//   * White rows on the Overview      = that person changed since you looked
//   * Boxed "NEW" in the header       = this page changed since your last visit; the
//     rows that changed are white until you leave the page
//   * Boxed "HOLD" / "OFFLINE"        = refresh frozen / last download failed
//
// EDGE CASES (each one is explained again next to the code that handles it):
//   * No Wi-Fi, no internet, slow or failed downloads -> the last good data stays
//     on screen, "OFFLINE" is shown, the green LED blinks, and it keeps retrying.
//   * Firebase errors (e.g. "Permission denied"), broken JSON, an empty /live
//     -> shown as an error or as 0 active people, never a crash.
//   * Odd values in the database (numbers stored as text, missing fields,
//     emoji / accents, very long text, the '|' character) -> cleaned up first.
//   * More people than fit on screen -> the first MAX_USERS are shown and the
//     Overview says "+N more"; nobody on screen at all -> "Waiting...".
//   * The person you are looking at stops exercising -> the page moves safely.
//   * A person's rep counts go back down (a new set) -> their streak restarts.
//   * Button bounce and long presses -> a hold never also counts as a tap.
//   * millis() wrapping back to 0 after ~49 days -> all timers still work.
//   * Every text buffer has a fixed size and is always cut off safely.

